# ifupdown2 ships ifup@.service but not the udev rule that starts it, so a
# re-enumerating USB NIC comes back named and link-up but without its address
# (Debian #988050). This supplies the missing trigger.
#
# Must match move as well as add. A re-enumerating NIC emits add (as eth0) then
# move (the rename to nic1); matching add alone loses the race, because the move
# event's property set overwrites SYSTEMD_WANTS before systemd acts on it.
#
# Numbered above 80 so 80-net-setup-link.rules has already set ID_NET_NAME from
# our .link file. Deliberately not named 80-ifupdown.rules — that would mask the
# real file under /lib if ifupdown2 ever ships it.
ACTION=="add|move", SUBSYSTEM=="net", ENV{ID_NET_NAME}=="{{ proxmox_fabric_interface }}", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="ifup@{{ proxmox_fabric_interface }}.service"
